315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 223 0 R
/E (This document specifies the software requirements for Project Management System, a web based application that allows a team to organize projects, manage tasks on a Kanban board, plan Agile sprints, track time and view project progress through a live analytics dashboard. This document covers the complete first version of the system and is intended to be the single reference for what the system must do. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 223 0 R
/T (1.2 Intended Audience and Reading Suggestions )
/E (1.2 Intended Audience and Reading Suggestions )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 223 0 R
/E (This document is intended for the development team building the system, the course instructor evaluating the project, and any reviewer who needs to understand the expected behaviour of the system. Section 2 gives an overall picture of the product. Section 3 covers external interfaces. Section 4 covers the analysis models. Section 5 lists the detailed functional requirements grouped by feature. Section 6 covers non functional, security and business rule requirements. The appendices contain the glossary, field layout and traceability matrix. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 223 0 R
/T (1.3 Product Scope )
/E (1.3 Product Scope )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 223 0 R
/E (Project Management System is a new, self contained web application. It allows a team to create workspaces and projects, break work into tasks and subtasks, plan work using an Agile backlog and sprints, log time against tasks, collaborate through comments and a live activity feed, and monitor progress through an analytics dashboard. Task updates are pushed to connected users in real time. The system is being built as a course mini project and is scoped for use by a small team rather than a large organisation. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
