<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 236 0 R
/E (time, add comment\) goes through REST; anything that must reach other already- connected users without a page refresh \(task moves, comments, notifications\) is additionally published to Django Channels over Redis and pushed to WebSocket clients. This keeps the REST API simple and cacheable while still meeting the real- time requirement \(FR-RTC-01\). )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
860 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 236 0 R
/E (The backend is deliberately built as a single deployable service organised into four internal modules by domain \(a "modular monolith"\) rather than four separate microservices, since SRS Section 2.6 scopes the system for a small team rather than production-scale, multi-service deployment; this keeps the six-sprint schedule in SRS Section 9 realistic while still keeping the modules independently testable, as required by NFR-005. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
