1105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 247 0 R
/E (A test item passes when every test case mapped to it in Section 15 produces its expected result with no severity-1 \(blocking\) or severity-2 \(major\) defect open against it. A feature fails acceptance if any functional requirement's test case fails, or if a security or performance test case fails against the thresholds stated in SRS Section 6. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 247 0 R
/T (5. Approach )
/E (5. Approach )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 247 0 R
/E (Testing follows the same black-box, requirement-driven approach used for validation planning in the SRS \(Section 8\): each functional requirement is exercised through the public REST/WebSocket API or the UI exactly as an end user would use it, rather than by inspecting internal code paths directly. Automated unit tests \(Pytest for the backend, Jest for the frontend\) run on every push through the Jenkins pipeline defined in SRS Section 10; integration and system tests are run before each sprint review; authorization tests are run for every role against every protected endpoint. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
